Package: fastRhockey
Title: Functions to Access Hockey Play by Play Data and Statistics
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ben", "Howell", , "benhowell71@gmail.com", role = "aut"),
    person("Saiem", "Gilani", , "saiem.gilani@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7194-9067")),
    person("Alyssa", "Longmuir", , "aklongmuir@gmail.com", role = "ctb"),
    person("fastRhockey authors", role = "cph")
  )
Description: A utility to scrape and load hockey play-by-play data and
    statistics. It covers the National Hockey League <https://www.nhl.com/>
    (the web API, the stats REST API, the Edge tracking API and the records
    API), the Professional Women's Hockey League <https://www.thepwhl.com/>,
    and the American Hockey League, Ontario Hockey League, Western Hockey
    League and Quebec Maritimes Junior Hockey League through their
    'HockeyTech' feeds. It also reads ESPN and Fox Sports NHL data, NCAA men's
    and women's hockey from ESPN, and 13 European leagues: Germany's DEL,
    Austria's ICE Hockey League, the United Kingdom's EIHL, Denmark's Metal
    Ligaen, the KHL, Russia's VHL, Sweden's SHL and HockeyAllsvenskan,
    Finland's Liiga, Switzerland's National League and Swiss Ice Hockey
    Federation competitions, Czechia's Extraliga and France's Ligue Magnus.
    Loaders read pre-scraped play-by-play, box score, schedule and
    expected-goals datasets from the 'SportsDataverse' data releases.
